	.globl	_silica_rt_actor_kill_abnormal
	.p2align	2
_silica_rt_actor_kill_abnormal:
; X0 = reference (held while the kill runs; an ended actor is :ok). Spec §15.1.2.3: kill_abnormal
; must not name the calling actor; the caller fails with :language_error and nothing is changed on
; it (a call it is serving gets no reply). The target is ended with reason tag 1
; (_silica_rt_actor_stop). When it is a row child the caller waits for its row's exit_done to
; carry the target's identity (its last act), then for the restart to settle
; (_silica_rt_supervisor_drain_ingress: the caller drains the supervisor's ingress itself unless
; it is a row child of that supervisor, which waits for the supervisor's thread to do it), so the
; replacement, when the policy makes one, exists when this returns. Both waits end at once when
; the caller itself is ended meanwhile (the target's :one_for_all or :rest_for_one cascade stops
; the caller): the target is dead or dying, :ok.
