; %bb.0: X0=actor_ref X1=level (0 low, 1 normal, 2 high; the emitter maps the program's atoms, and
; any other value is normal, as on the board) -> X0 = 0 (:ok) or 1 (:actor_not_found: a null
; reference, or an actor that has ended, spec §22.10). The level is stored in ACB #520 for every
; actor (item N stage 4): for a carrier actor it is the run queue the actor is pushed to at its
; next push and its weight class under :weighted_fair and :lottery (prims_actors_carrier_asm,
; _silica_rt_rq_push; an actor already queued stays where it is, the board's rule). A dangerous
; actor, on a thread of its own, keeps the level and nothing reads it: the OS schedules its thread
; (the pthread QoS mapping of the thread-per-actor runtime is gone).
