; The registry slot count of this image: one slot per atom of the build (atoms/atom_table.silica
; build_runtime_atom_table; actor_memory_budget_plan.md item J). Atoms are interned when the program
; is built (spec §4.1.7), so the tables never overflow. The keyed forms treat an int64 below this
; count as an atom and at or above it as an actor_ref: control blocks are calloc'd, and no hosted
; heap hands out addresses that low (macOS: above 0x1_0000_0000; Linux non-PIE: above the image).
	.section	__DATA,__const
	.p2align	3
	.globl	_silica_registry_slots
