; PID registry primitive actor (spec §20.3.1).
; State layout: one calloc block of _silica_registry_slots * 16 B: occ[slots] (int64, 1 = held) at +0,
; actor_ref words[slots] at +slots*8. The same block is read directly by the keyed forms and by
; _silica_rt_register_actor_named (the store writes the ref before the occ word; a removal clears
; the occ word first).
; Message record layout follows record emission: shape word@0, op@8, name@16, pid@24.
; Behavior return layout follows actor runtime convention: tag@0, reply@8, next_state@16.
; :insert replies :ok (stored, or the actor already holds this very name), :name_taken (a live actor
; or supervisor holds the name), :already_registered (the actor holds another name in this table) or
; :actor_not_found (the actor has ended); the reply is a (status atom, actor_ref) pair.
