; The startup code installs the handlers before main runs (spec §15.4.5.5): dyld calls every
; __mod_init_func entry before main, so a fault in main's prologue, or in anything else that runs
; before main's body, is reported like any other. The calls from spawn and from main's prologue remain
; and return at once (the installed flag); spawn's call is also what gives an actor thread its handler
; state on hosts where that differs.
